    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi's pencil was 12.5 cm and Anu's was 12.45 cm.\n\"Whose is longer?\" asked their teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "tenths",
     "hundredths",
     "equivalent decimal"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To compare decimals, compare the whole part first, then the tenths, then the hundredths. 12.5 is the same as 12.50, and 50 hundredths is more than 45, so 12.5 is greater than 12.45.\nA decimal can be written as a fraction: 0.25 is 25/100 which is 1/4. A fraction can be changed to a decimal by dividing: 3/4 is 0.75.\nAdding zeros at the end of a decimal does not change its value."
    }
   },
